3. INTERFACE WITH THE SUBBOX CLIENT

The Subbox client application (https://github.com/laker-93/subbox-app) is a
separate program, licensed under the GNU General Public License v3.0. It
communicates with this Software only over a network HTTP API, at arm's length,
as two independent programs exchanging data.

That HTTP interface is a boundary, not a linkage. This Software is not a
derivative work of the Subbox client, and the GPL-3.0 that governs the client
does not extend to this Software.

The definitions of the HTTP API itself — endpoint paths, request and response
schemas — are interface specifications and may be freely implemented by anyone.


